From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:06:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/aom_film_grain: Assume the predicted luma point bound

The predicted luma path copies num_y_points from the reference set
before it indexes res[14] and y_points[14]. The reference is always the
first set of the same payload, which cannot use prediction itself and
whose count was checked against 14 when it was parsed. gcc 15.2 with
-march=x86-64-v3 does not carry that bound into this loop and reports a
stringop-overflow warning.

State the bound with av_assume(). With assertions enabled it is checked
like av_assert0(); otherwise it is a compiler hint and adds no branch.
av_assert1() would expand to nothing at the default assert level and
leave the warning in place.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
---
 libavcodec/aom_film_grain.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavcodec/aom_film_grain.c b/libavcodec/aom_film_grain.c
index bb60c5577418131a5a8c1bf2e23997f0f18025cc..ffe0f471a508b1f72c41b696e39023969eaba63d 100644
--- a/libavcodec/aom_film_grain.c
+++ b/libavcodec/aom_film_grain.c
@@ -225,6 +225,8 @@ int ff_aom_parse_film_grain_sets(AVFilmGrainAFGS1Params *s,
             if (bits_res) {
                 int res[14], pred, granularity;
                 aom->num_y_points = ref->codec.aom.num_y_points;
+                // ref is the first set, which cannot predict and whose count was checked when parsed
+                av_assume(aom->num_y_points <= 14);
                 for (i = 0; i < aom->num_y_points; i++)
                     res[i] = get_bits(gb, bits_res);
                 granularity = get_bits(gb, 3);
